     "text": "Diaz-Roberts Medical Group\nRe: Bobby Carson (DOB 07/30/1972)\n\nNovember 08, 2024: Mr. Bobby Carson was seen today for follow-up regarding his Prostate adenocarcinoma, high grade. During this visit, his blood pressure was recorded at 139/82, and he weighed 165 pounds. He continues to do well, and there are no new concerns. The patient is taking leuprolide 7.5 mg as prescribed. His latest results from Heritage Diagnostic Services on December 8, 2012, indicated a total cholesterol of 276 and HDL of 71, with a fructosamine level of 232. There was no nicotine metabolite detected, and gamma-glutamyl transferase (GGT) was 24.\n\nDecember 02, 2023: Mr. Carson visited on December 02, 2023, to address a rash. His blood pressure at that time was 141/79, and his weight was 154 pounds. Mr. Carson has a known history of Prostate adenocarcinoma, high grade, which was treated approximately 20.2 years with a Gleason score of 9. There is no current evidence of active and he remains stable.\n\nDecember 24, 2022: On December 24, 2022, Mr. Carson was seen for follow-up regarding his Prostate adenocarcinoma, high grade. His blood pressure was 145/88, and he weighed 156 pounds at that visit. The patient is doing well and has no new complaints. The treatment with leuprolide 7.5 mg continues to be effective. \n\nSocial history reveals that Mr. Carson used to smoke cigarettes at a rate of approximately half a pack per day, starting from March 14, 1997, and he quit smoking on October 02, 2023. He reports consuming about 12 alcoholic drinks per week. His mother had myocardial infarction at age 49 and passed away at 52. His mother also has a history of hypertension and is currently alive at 75 years old. \n\nThe patient's medical record reflects a comprehensive management plan for his Prostate adenocarcinoma, high grade, which has been effectively controlled with ongoing treatment. We will continue to monitor his condition closely. \n\nDr. Louis Leonard\nOncology, Diaz-Roberts Medical Group\n"
